    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py` and wrote 18 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. All of them pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nThe function validates the inputs first: `start` must be a plain `date`, `n` must be an `int` (not a `bool` or `float`), and every holiday must be a plain `date`. Any other type raises `TypeError`, including a `datetime` anywhere a `date` is expected. It then steps one day at a time to the `n`-th business day, skipping weekends and holidays. For `n == 0` it returns `start` if that's a business day, otherwise the next one. The tests cover forward and backward movement, weekend and holiday starts, the `n == 0` cases, generator holidays, weekend holidays having no effect, and the `TypeError` cases.",
